note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note stats.om (lane EvalStats, spark-rsi-mv #73): the REUSE-1 statistics and decision unit.
note Contract: omega-mv d6edaad1 docs/reuse/REUSE-1.md (sections 6, 9, 10); evaluator formats:
note docs EVAL-FORMATS (split directory, raw run log, proc.log, acq.log, controls.log K7, seeds K6).
note No fn main here: the evaluator dispatcher calls stmain. Names: functions st*, globals ST*,
note constants SK*. turing.om and receipt.om reuse the st* output, path and file helpers.
note
note CLI (argv[1] is the dispatcher's subcommand and is not read):
note   stats SPLITDIR RUNDIR CTRLDIR SEEDHEX OUTDIR
note SPLITDIR = the FINAL split directory (index, sessions, gNN.exp); RUNDIR = arm-A-rep-R-gNN.log,
note proc.log, acq.log; CTRLDIR = the directory holding controls.log, or - when no control run
note exists (every control then counts as not run); SEEDHEX = the 32-byte FINAL seed as 64 hex;
note OUTDIR receives stats.txt (the report, also written to stdout) and stats.sum (words below).
note Exit 0 = report written (the decision is inside it), 2 = inputs refused (status=REFUSED line
note with a code, nothing else decided), other = output write failure.
note
note Definitions (all integer, no floating point):
note  - reps R = 3 (0-based in names and logs), arms 0 echo 1 full 2 cache 3 method 4 delta
note    5 idelta 6 deltap 7 select. Library charged per arm: method, delta, select = acq lib 1
note    (TRAIN), deltap = lib 2 (TRAINP), every other arm none (idelta runs with LIBDIR -).
note  - cost of one arm process (arm a, rep r, group g) = start-to-ready (proc word 3, which
note    includes request 0's round trip) + sum of round trips of requests 1.. of the group. This
note    charges start-to-ready to the first request (contract 5.4).
note  - V(a, g) = sum over the 3 reps of the process cost; acq(a) = sum over the 3 reps of the
note    elapsed ns of the arm's library build. T(a) = sum over groups of V(a, g) + acq(a). Sums over
note    reps stand for the per-group means of contract 10 (the factor 3 cancels in every ratio).
note  - rho(a) = T(a) / T(full); ratio rho(x)/rho(y) = T(x) / T(y) (full cancels, same resample).
note    Statistic s: 0..7 rho(arm s); 8 delta/cache; 9 delta/idelta; 10 select/delta;
note    11 delta/method; 12 idelta/full.
note  - ppm = floor(num * 1000000 / den), exact 128-bit product and division. Floor makes the
note    decision comparisons exact: ppm < 1000000 iff ratio < 1; ppm >= 1000000 iff ratio >= 1.
note  - bootstrap: B = 10000 resamples; resample b draws G group indices, each = splitmix64() mod G
note    (bias below G / 2^64); one draw serves every arm (paired); splitmix64 state starts at the
note    FINAL seed bytes 0..7 read little endian (contract 10, K6) and is advanced once per draw.
note    The 10000 values of each statistic are sorted ascending; interval = (v[k_lo], v[k_hi]) with
note    nearest rank k = ceil(p * B) - 1 (0-based): p = 0.025 gives k_lo = 249, p = 0.975 gives 9749.
note    The point value is the statistic on the sample itself (every group once).
note  - quantiles: nearest rank on ascending values, index ceil(p * m / 100) - 1 for p = 50, 95, 99,
note    over the QUERY round trips (all 3 reps) of one arm, cold (exp cold flag 1) or warm (0),
note    per category: all, session type, novelty class, family, n class. m = 0 prints na.
note  - cat_rho: request round trips only (no start-to-ready, no acquisition), per session category,
note    arm over full; regime lines are the cat_rho ratios delta/method and idelta/full per type.
note  - correctness: the log's word 15 is recomputed from words 5..11 (QUERY 1 iff status, r0, r1
note    equal; other requests 2 iff status equal; echo 2); a record is wrong when either the log or
note    the recomputation says 0; disagreements are counted as log_inconsistent. Echo is never scored.
note  - transfer coverage: delta-arm QUERYs (all reps) in sessions of novelty class 2 with route 3
note    or 4, over all such QUERYs. Fallback = route 5 among an arm's QUERYs.
note  - payback(a): FINAL request order (group 0.., request 0..), per request the rep-summed
note    (full - arm) cost (request 0 = start-to-ready); the number of QUERYs seen when the cumulative
note    sum first exceeds acq(a); none if it never does.
note  - Cbar (contract 6, #744), per arm, ppm of one full QUERY: F = floor(full QUERY round-trip
note    sum / count); r = echo mean QUERY / F; q = QUERYs not served by routes 2..4 / QUERYs;
note    e = mean of the route 2..4 QUERYs / F - r; K = acq(a) / F (full-QUERY units); N = the arm's
note    QUERYs over 3 reps; cbar = r + (1 - q) e + q + K / N (signed, truncating toward zero);
note    observed = (QUERY round-trip sum + acq) / N / F. Reported, never in the decision.
note  - echo_sub(a) = (T(a) - T(echo)) / (T(full) - T(echo)), signed ppm (secondary figure).
note  - decision (contract 10, K7): STOP on any wrong answer or wrong refusal of arms 1..7, a control
note    with outcome 0 or the served-tampered flag, or lower bound of rho(delta) >= 1; else GO when
note    upper bounds of rho(delta), delta/cache and delta/idelta are < 1, transfer coverage >= 1/2
note    (with at least one transfer QUERY) and every control C1..C12 has records and none not run;
note    else INVESTIGATE. Every failing condition is listed as a reason line.
note
note stats.sum: 256 words LE. 0 magic 3544386041195737426 (R1STS001), 1 version 1, 2 decision
note (1 GO, 2 INVESTIGATE, 3 STOP), 3 reason bits (0 wrong_answer, 1 wrong_refusal,
note 2 control_undetected, 3 tampered_served, 4 rho_delta_lower_ge_1, 5 rho_delta_upper_ge_1,
note 6 delta_over_cache_upper_ge_1, 7 delta_over_idelta_upper_ge_1, 8 transfer_coverage_below_half,
note 9 control_not_run), 4 groups, 5 sessions, 6 requests, 7 queries (per rep), 8 reps, 9 split id,
note 10 bootstrap seed, 11 resamples, 12 scored QUERY responses (arms 1..7, all reps), 13 correct
note ones, 14 wrong ones, 15 wrong refusals, 16 transfer QUERYs, 17 covered, 18..21 holdout digest
note (index words 7..10 as stored), 22 log inconsistencies, 24 + 3 s .. 26 + 3 s point, lo, hi ppm
note of statistic s (s 0..12), 64 + a T(a), 72 + a acq(a), 80 + a route-5 QUERYs of arm a,
note 88 + a payback QUERYs (18446744073709551615 = none or not applicable); the rest 0.
note
note Refusal codes: 1 usage, 2 index unreadable, 3 index invalid, 4 sessions invalid, 5 exp invalid,
note 6 log missing, 7 log size, 8 log identity words, 9 log expectation words differ from exp,
note 10 proc.log invalid, 11 proc record missing or duplicate, 12 acq.log invalid or a needed build
note missing, 13 controls.log invalid, 14 capacity, 15 output write failed.

